         reading : The spatial shift current is a divergenceless vector field on the static branch: its flux through any closed surface (including spheres at infinity) is zero.  No Gauss-map charge exists in the Noether current.
  [PASS] R4 [canonical momentum is J^0 by another name] pi = dL/d phidot = f'(K) phidot 
         measured: pi = f'(0)*0 = 0
         reading : The canonical momentum of the shift direction IS the charge density (pi = J^0 in the static frame up to metric factors).  It vanishes for the same reason J^0 does.

